# Template Adaptation Plan: WebUni to Tutoring Portal

## Overview
This plan outlines the steps to transform the "WebUni" LMS template into a Personal Tutoring Website. The core design aesthetic (colors, typography, layout) will be preserved, but the content model and functionality will be shifted from "Static Course Consumption" to "Interactive Tutor Booking".

## 1. Terminology & Concept Mapping

| Original Template Concept | Tutoring Website Concept | Notes |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Course** | **Learning Session** / **Tutor Profile** | Instead of buying a video course, users book a live session or view a tutor. |
| **Category** | **Subject / Domain** | e.g., Math, Science, Coding vs. Web Design, Photography. |
| **Teacher / Author** | **Tutor** | The primary entity users interact with. |
| **Student Count** | **Sessions Completed** / **Reviews** | Social proof metrics. |
| **Price** | **Hourly Rate** | Cost per hour or per session. |
| **"Buy This Course"** | **"Book Session"** | Call to Action. |
| **Blog / News** | **Learning Resources** | Articles or tips from tutors. |

## 2. Page-Specific Adaptations

### A. Home Page ([index.html](file:///D:/final%20year%20project/V/work%20temp/webuni-gh-pages/index.html))
-   **Hero Section**: 
    -   *Current*: "Get The Best Free Online Courses" + Signup Form.
    -   *New*: "Find Your Perfect Tutor" + Search Form (Subject, Location/Online).
-   **Categories Section**:
    -   *Current*: "IT Development", "Photography".
    -   *New*: "Popular Subjects" (Mathematics, Physics, Computer Science).
-   **Featured Courses Section**:
    -   *Current*: Grid of courses with price.
    -   *New*: Grid of **Featured Tutors**. 
    -   *Data*: Show Tutor Name, Subject Specialization, Hourly Rate, Rating.
-   **Signup Section**:
    -   *Current*: "Sign up to become a teacher".
    -   *New*: "Become a Tutor" (Functionally similar, just text changes).

### B. Listing Page ([courses.html](file:///D:/final%20year%20project/V/work%20temp/webuni-gh-pages/courses.html) -> `tutors.html`)
-   **Filters**:
    -   *Current*: All, Finance, Design...
    -   *New*: All, Math, Science, Languages, Coding.
-   **Grid Items**:
    -   Display Tutor Cards instead of Course Cards.
    -   Clicking an item goes to the Tutor Profile.

### C. Detail Page ([single-course.html](file:///D:/final%20year%20project/V/work%20temp/webuni-gh-pages/single-course.html) -> `tutor-profile.html`)
-   **Header / Meta Area**:
    -   *Current*: Course Title, Teacher Name, Category.
    -   *New*: **Tutor Name**, **Tagline** (e.g., "Expert in Calculus & Algebra"), **Rating**, **Hourly Rate**.
-   **Main Content Tabs**:
    -   *Current*: Description, Certification, Instructor.
    -   *New*: **About Me**, **Teaching Style**, **Schedule/Availability**.
-   **Sidebar**:
    -   *Current*: Price, Buy Button.
    -   *New*: **Book a Free Trial**, **SendMessage**.

## 3. Style & Layout Adjustments
-   **Color Usage**: Keep the `#d82a4e` (Pink/Red) as the primary action color (Booking buttons).
-   **Icons**: Ensure icons (FontAwesome) match the new context (e.g., use `fa-user`, `fa-calendar`, `fa-video-camera` instead of `fa-file-text`).

## 4. Implementation Steps
1.  **Clean up**: Remove unused elements (e.g., if there's a cart or checkout meant for digital goods).
2.  **Rename**: Rename files to reflect new purpose ([courses.html](file:///D:/final%20year%20project/V/work%20temp/webuni-gh-pages/courses.html) -> `tutors.html`).
3.  **Content Replacement**: Update HTML text and images to match the Tutoring domain.
4.  **Component Tweaking**: Modify the "Course Item" HTML structure to better display Tutor attributes (e.g., round profile picture getting more prominence).

## 5. Verification
-   Check responsiveness on mobile (Hero section and Helper grids).
-   Ensure all links navigate correctly to the new pages.
